Subject: [PATCH] tegra: enforce OOT graphics and mainline BPMP ownership

The ordinary Tegra194 BPMP transport and its boot-critical clock, reset,
and power-domain providers are supplied by the built-in mainline driver.
The OOT tegra_bpmp module contains the hypervisor transport and only matches
the tegra186-bpmp-hv and tegra194-safe-bpmp-hv compatibles.

Allow non-hypervisor builds to omit that module without dropping ivc_ext,
which is independently consumed by other OOT drivers.

The same provider split disables the in-tree TEGRA_HOST1X option. Preserve
its default security-firewall setting in the exclusive OOT host1x provider,
where the dependent Kconfig symbol is otherwise unavailable.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [local provider-ownership policy]

diff --git a/nvidia-oot/drivers/firmware/tegra/Makefile b/nvidia-oot/drivers/firmware/tegra/Makefile
--- a/nvidia-oot/drivers/firmware/tegra/Makefile
+++ b/nvidia-oot/drivers/firmware/tegra/Makefile
@@ -8,7 +8,9 @@
 obj-m		+= ivc_ext.o
+ifneq ($(NV_OOT_BPMP_SKIP_BUILD),y)
 tegra_bpmp-y	+= ../../clk/tegra/clk-bpmp.o
 tegra_bpmp-y	+= ../../reset/tegra/reset-bpmp.o
 tegra_bpmp-y	+= ../../soc/tegra/powergate-bpmp.o
 tegra_bpmp-$(CONFIG_DEBUG_FS)	+= bpmp-debugfs.o
 tegra_bpmp-y	+= bpmp-tegra186-hv.o
-obj-m 		+= tegra_bpmp.o
\ No newline at end of file
+obj-m 		+= tegra_bpmp.o
+endif

diff --git a/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/host1x/Makefile b/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/host1x/Makefile
--- a/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/host1x/Makefile
+++ b/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/host1x/Makefile
@@ -2,6 +2,8 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
 # Copyright (c) 2022-2024, NVIDIA CORPORATION.  All rights reserved.
 
+ccflags-y += -DCONFIG_TEGRA_HOST1X_FIREWALL
+
 host1x-y = \
 	bus.o \
 	syncpt.o \
